# Rhythm Sync Teacher

## Product docs

Before large changes, read:

- `docs/spec.md` — product scope and release goals
- `docs/architecture.md` — module boundaries and data flow
- `docs/acceptance.md` — Definition of Done checks

## Stack

- Vite + React + TypeScript
- Web Audio metronome, MediaPipe Pose (`@mediapipe/tasks-vision`)
- No backend unless the user explicitly asks

## Boundaries

- Rhythm logic lives only in `src/lib/` (`metronome`, `pose`, `stompDetector`, `scorer`, `stickFigure`)
- UI components render state and forward events; they do not compute hit/miss
- Unit tests cover `src/lib/*` with synthetic data; do not require a real camera or MediaPipe in unit tests

## Out of scope unless asked

- Music upload / beat detection
- Accounts, cloud sync, native mobile apps
- New exercise types not listed in `docs/spec.md`

## UI

- Russian copy for user-facing strings
- Keep the existing visual language (Space Grotesk / DM Sans, warm-teal palette)

## Git

- Do not commit or push unless the user asks
- Prefer small commits aligned with one feature slice
